# Server security & DTOs

Never trust the client. Check `session.authenticated` and building membership / permissions on **every** mutating method.

## Endpoints

- Default `requireLogin => true` except explicitly public methods
- Scopes: super-admin, owner, employee roles (orders, payments, kitchen) — match domain docs
- Employees are scoped to assigned buildings; customers only see their own data
- Log failures with `session.log`; do not leak internals in client messages

## Models

- Table models stay internal; expose **protocol** types for create/update/read
- `*Create` / `*Update` DTOs: only writable fields (no `id`, no server-only flags, no other users' ids unless required)
- Responses: smallest safe shape (ids, display fields). Omit secrets, hashes, unused relations
- Prefer explicit exceptions (`Exception` in `.spy.yaml`) over generic strings

Change `.spy.yaml` and endpoints — never `lib/src/generated/` or `sip_sync_client`.

See `.cursor/skills/sip-sync-security-and-errors/SKILL.md`.
